diff --git a/NO_SMOOTH.md b/NO_SMOOTH.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7c5fa53
--- /dev/null
+++ b/NO_SMOOTH.md
@@ -0,0 +1,121 @@
+# Per-Graphics noSmooth extension
+
+Based on Processing libprocessing `0b1a55dd2010a7f170b010ac5fceb48aed7f8d9e`,
+with its locked Processing Bevy fork (`9da7c625`, Bevy 0.19 development snapshot).
+No AviUtl2, CEF or JavaScript adapter code is added to this library.
+
+```rust
+use processing::prelude::*;
+init(Config::default())?;
+let surface = surface_create_offscreen(1920, 1080, 1., TextureFormat::Rgba8UnormSrgb)?;
+let graphics = graphics_create(surface, 1920, 1080, TextureFormat::Rgba8UnormSrgb)?;
+graphics_no_smooth(graphics)?;
+graphics_begin_draw(graphics)?;
+// graphics_record_command(...)
+graphics_end_draw(graphics)?;
+let frame = graphics_readback_completed_raw(graphics)?;
+// frame.bytes: tightly packed rows, width * 4 bytes for RGBA8.
+exit(0)?; // Drop the Bevy App/GPU resources before thread-local destruction.
+```
+
+The independent APIs are `graphics_set_antialiasing(g, Antialiasing::Off)` and
+`graphics_set_image_sampling(g, ImageSampling::Nearest)`. All return the existing
+`processing_core::error::Result`. Unknown C/WASM numeric modes return
+`InvalidArgument`; nonexistent Graphics return `GraphicsNotFound`.
+
+| Setting | Meaning |
+| --- | --- |
+| Antialiasing::Default / C value 0 | Existing Bevy MSAA default, four samples |
+| Antialiasing::Off / C value 1 | `Msaa::Off`, one sample, not zero |
+| ImageSampling::Default / C value 0 | Inherit the individual image's sampler |
+| ImageSampling::Linear / C value 1 | Override mag/min/mipmap filters with Linear |
+| ImageSampling::Nearest / C value 2 | Override mag/min/mipmap filters with Nearest |
+
+Configure before the first `begin_draw`, recorded command or flush. The internal
+three-frame initialization warmup does not lock configuration. Changing settings
+after recording starts returns `InvalidArgument` and changes neither setting.
+There is no dynamic frame-boundary switching in this version. Create a new
+Graphics to use another configuration. Leaving both settings unspecified retains
+the old rendering path, sampler and automatic dithering.
+
+An explicit Graphics filter takes precedence over `image_set_sampler`'s filter.
+The source descriptor's wrapping, LOD and comparison settings remain intact.
+Nearest sets anisotropy to one because wgpu disallows anisotropic Nearest filters.
+Aliases are cached per Graphics/source descriptor. They share the uploaded GPU
+texture and view, with their own sampler; the original image is never modified.
+Placeholder assets have MAIN_WORLD usage only, so no duplicate GPU texture or
+image upload is allocated. Aliases refresh their shared texture reference when
+the source GPU asset is replaced. Destroying Graphics releases aliases/samplers.
+
+`Off` or `Nearest` also disables Bevy's automatic `DebandDither`: otherwise an
+opaque two-color image may acquire 254 instead of 255 color values. Returning to
+Default/Linear before the first draw restores the prior dither component. This
+does not disable explicitly requested blur, bloom, filters or custom shaders.
+
+For explicitly configured Graphics, an initial `BackgroundColor` uses the camera
+render-pass clear instead of a fullscreen mesh. It removes one draw and puts the
+background before alpha blending. Subsequent backgrounds within the same command
+stream retain the upstream mesh behavior. Explicitly sampled image materials
+honor texture alpha via AlphaMode::Blend, including the user's blend-state
+override; opaque images remain opaque. The unspecified legacy image-material
+behavior is retained. Arbitrary custom materials retain their own sampler rules.
+
+Builtin filled/stroked text uses Parley layout, Skrifa outlines and Lyon meshes;
+its raster edge coverage follows camera MSAA. Lines, circles and tessellated
+shapes use the same camera. Camera3d MSAA specialization controls standard 3D
+color/depth/resolve sample counts as well. Custom shaders, particle-specific
+renderers, SDF text and external bitmap text may contain their own smoothing;
+disabling camera MSAA does not promise to remove that. Bitmap text already has
+alpha in its pixels. Preserve it; do not threshold every alpha channel.
+
+GPU RGBA8 readback is in the chosen Graphics format. For the tested
+`Rgba8UnormSrgb` render target and ordinary alpha blending, RGB is sRGB encoded
+after linear-space compositing, while alpha is linear coverage. Transparent
+composited RGB therefore contains linear-premultiplied color encoded as sRGB.
+Decode RGB to linear before unpremultiplying for a straight-alpha consumer;
+divide only when alpha is nonzero, then re-encode to sRGB. Row pitch is stripped
+by `graphics_readback_completed_raw`. Do not interpret RGBA16F/HDR data as RGBA8.
+REPLACE or arbitrary custom blend states can change this RGB/alpha relationship;
+an adapter must define its output-alpha contract for those modes separately.
+
+The old `graphics_readback_raw` still flushes pending commands. The new completed
+readback API reads the last render without another app update, and intentionally
+does not execute queued commands. Use it after `graphics_flush`/`end_draw` to avoid
+two render updates per frame. GPU wait/readback remains synchronous and stays on
+the initialization thread.
+
+Build and verify on Windows:
+
+```powershell
+git submodule update --init --depth 1
+cargo build --locked --release --example no_smooth_verify --example smooth_probe
+.\target\release\examples\no_smooth_verify.exe proof-images
+.\target\release\examples\smooth_probe.exe 1920 1080 shapes proof-default 120 default
+.\target\release\examples\smooth_probe.exe 1920 1080 shapes proof-off 120 no-smooth
+cargo check --locked --release -p processing_ffi -p processing_wasm
+cargo test --locked --release -p processing_ffi --lib smoothing_abi_tests
+```
+
+`processing_ffi/include/processing.h` is generated by cbindgen. The C commands are
+`processing_graphics_set_antialiasing`, `processing_graphics_set_image_sampling`
+and `processing_graphics_no_smooth`; they use `processing_check_error` and clear
+old errors like existing commands. See `examples/no_smooth.c`. WASM names are
+`graphicsSetAntialiasing`, `graphicsSetImageSampling`, `graphicsNoSmooth`.
+WASM wrappers are added but unverified: this crate is gated by `target_arch=wasm32`,
+so a Windows cargo check does not type-check their bodies. The wasm32 target is
+not installed in the tested environment; neither the WASM build nor browser
+execution has been verified. Python bindings are unchanged in this native-first
+extension.
+
+The GPU verification checks actual readback bytes: AA edges, outline text,
+two-color Nearest scaling, independently configured/shared images, Repeat
+wrapping, shared GPU texture identities, Graphics blitting/composition, fill and
+image alpha, late-command errors, completed-readback semantics, destruction,
+recreation and GPU image counts. Benchmark CSV stages separate command creation,
+CPU tessellation/submission, and readback including remaining GPU execution wait.
+They are wall times, not GPU timestamp-query durations. First frame, initialization
+and Graphics creation/warmup are recorded separately.
+
+Processing-style noSmooth differs from p5.js Canvas2D (image interpolation only)
+and p5.js WebGL (geometry AA only). No p5.js script automatically runs through
+this Rust library. A JavaScript runtime and command adapter are a separate layer.
